WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.360
Hi, I'm Sian from BBC Learning English.

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:06.020
Today, I'm going to give you five uses of the verb 'get'.

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:09.220
So you get five lessons for the price of one!

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:13.000
Number one – get can mean buy or obtain.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.820
I got myself a new phone last weekend.

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:19.080
Number two – get can mean receive.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:20.580
I just got a message.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:23.540
Number three –

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:27.340
get with an adjective can mean become.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:31.140
Ugh! So many messages! I'm getting really annoyed!

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:35.100
Number four – get can also mean understand.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.660
Hang on, someone's just sent me a joke…

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:42.120
I don't get it!

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:43.480
‘In tents!’

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:45.120
I get it!

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:48.300
Number five - get can also mean arrive.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.900
I need to get home early so I'm off!

